decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.54$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.54$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/30/30d1e296e7c83fa8925feb116c9035de14790e89ddad37ab44710feacadf13a8.png)\n\nAs $t\\to \\infty ,$ the curve\n{{field-5}}.\nSo, we have\n{{field-6}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-7}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-8}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe {{field-9}} of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/05/054b319170c634494c703d9588419cb6e44414196c970ca0c39689bc62f90d97.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ y={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.54$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.54$ | $0.59$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/30/30d1e296e7c83fa8925feb116c9035de14790e89ddad37ab44710feacadf13a8.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ and ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{converges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/05/054b319170c634494c703d9588419cb6e44414196c970ca0c39689bc62f90d97.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166942 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ae65751-95a4-59cf-8378-ff6dcd4e1cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427032} {:answer/id #uuid "9187d439-6066-5341-b833-bfb001eced5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9187d439-6066-5341-b833-bfb001eced5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427044} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fe24b1-f8bf-5e58-ba73-46d45bbacc6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1603c7b9-db79-5f4e-aaaa-8db20bd28197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426988} {:answer/id #uuid "c6235c16-97de-5d7d-9ce8-5b49098e30d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1603c7b9-db79-5f4e-aaaa-8db20bd28197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426988} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b392be-6bfe-5887-a4ae-2c2f7f38f0c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f6c408e-5799-5dd6-95a6-0b30e664deef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426984} {:answer/id #uuid "b15096fa-69b5-5355-ab90-8ce11789ee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15096fa-69b5-5355-ab90-8ce11789ee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427060} :answer-field/id #uuid "b43329db-c49b-5cae-a0d0-88d411d89292" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ec8fdd-f2bd-5e00-9ccf-554874baea46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427007} {:answer/id #uuid "4b49be0e-41f7-5533-aa09-d1989f6eb279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427010} {:answer/id #uuid "959c41db-5092-586d-aab2-9a137d9f4150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ec8fdd-f2bd-5e00-9ccf-554874baea46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427007} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3854fdb-754f-5225-8e33-2513e7fb53ca" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09d0be6c-5113-5622-999f-8ea781b16416" :question/math-academy-id "q-334269" :question/problem "![](images/ff/ffa777ecd1ebf6594ca87b2d41e804cc4170daad58cf94aa7dc56d0be92e0a58.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i},$ where $a,b\\in R,$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that the given curve is $\\text{bounded}$ (and closed), representing $\\text{an ellipse}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nBut we have that:\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a>0,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a<0.$\n\nThus, we must have $a=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166942 :knowled